    "content": "あなたは英語学習コンテンツの独立評価者です。以下の英語記事から「英語上級者が学ぶ価値のあるKey Phrase」を選ぶ課題があり、\n複数の匿名の選定結果(セット S1〜Sn、各5件以内)があります。各候補を下記rubricで採点してください。どのセットがどのモデルの結果かは不明です。\n\n【選定時に参加者へ与えられた条件(参考)】\n1. 本文中の連続した語句だけを抜き出す(一般化以外の変更・言い換え・追加・創作は禁止)。\n2. 一般化後5語以内。\n3. 固有名詞や特定の人物・物事を指す部分は、意味と文法を保って ~ / A / B / someone / something 等に置き換える(一般化できる場合は必ず行う)。\n4. 上級者でも学ぶ価値のある語彙・イディオム・慣用表現を優先する。\n5. 基本語だけで構成され字面どおりに意味が分かる表現や、上級者なら知っている易しい表現は除外する。\n6. 条件を満たす候補から5件選ぶ。適切な候補が不足する場合のみ5件未満とし、数合わせはしない。\n\n【採点rubric(各候補、各0〜2の整数)】\n- G 一般化の適切さ: 2=本文固有の固有名詞・特定の人物/物事が適切に一般化されている、または一般化すべき要素がなく原文のままで適切 / 1=一般化が不十分または過剰、あるいは軽微な不自然さ / 0=一般化すべき固有要素が残って学習価値を損なう、または一般化で意味・文法が壊れている。\n- V 上級者向け学習価値: 2=上級者でも学ぶ価値が明確(句動詞・イディオム・コロケーション・語法・語彙として) / 1=価値はあるが中程度、または一部平易 / 0=学習価値がほぼない。\n- E 易しさの排除: 2=易しい表現ではない(意味が字面から自明でない) / 1=やや易しいが慣用的な意味や語法の学びはある / 0=基本語のみで字面どおり、上級者なら当然知っている。\n- N 単位の自然さ: 2=自然で完結した学習単位 / 1=余分な語または不足があるが許容 / 0=中途半端に切られている・不自然。\n- needs_generalization: その候補の元の表現に、一般化(~, A/B, someone, something等)すべき要素が本文上あったか(true/false)。\nセット単位: padding = 5件を埋めるために学習価値の低い候補(V<=0またはE<=0)を入れていると判断するか(true/false)。\n\n【注意】\n- 本文との一致・語数は別途機械検証するため、ここでは採点対象外。ただし本文に明らかに存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ noteに \"not_in_text\" と書く。\n- 候補の優劣を、セットの並び順やセットIDから推測しない。各候補を独立に採点する。\n- 候補が0件のセットは candidates を空配列にする。\n\n【出力】JSONのみ(説明文・コードフェンス不要)。noteは通常は空文字、本文に存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ \"not_in_text\"。形式:\n{\"sets\":[{\"set_id\":\"S1\",\"padding\":false,\"candidates\":[{\"idx\":1,\"G\":2,\"V\":2,\"E\":1,\"N\":2,\"needs_generalization\":false,\"note\":\"\"}]}]}\n\n\n【記事】\n\n# “Can’t Wait for the Next Episode”? Make One Yourself? “byUs” Lets You Shape Stories with Characters You Love\n\n“Wait, it ends here!?” Have you ever blurted that out when a manga ends at an exciting moment and says the story will continue next time? What will that character say next? What will happen to the two of them? It might be a shame to let those ideas stay only in your head.\n\nThe company that runs LINE Manga has announced the launch of “byUs,” an AI story chat service. It is pronounced “bias.” You can enjoy talking with your favorite characters and make your own stories based on the works. You can take a step from the reader’s seat onto the stage of story-making.\n\nIf you thought, “Can’t you already talk with characters?” you’ve noticed something important. LINE Manga already has “Character Chat.” The company says the difference is that, as well as having conversations, you can make stories more freely. In other words, you can enjoy not only asking, “What should we talk about next?” but also, “What should happen next?”\n\nFor example, you can continue an official story in the service. Or you can make your own story as a fan. “What if that person showed up here?” “If it were me, I’d want to see this happen.” The ideas that grew with every turn of the page can now become a starting point for your own stories. The time spent waiting for what happens next may become time spent thinking up what happens next.\n\nWhat’s more, you can publish the fan stories you make if you want to. You can enjoy them privately, or let someone else read them. But things change when you make a story public. “Will people understand this plot?” “I want to work on what happens next a little more.” You may find yourself thinking like a story-maker before you know it, even though you started out as a reader.\n\nOf course, you can’t bring in just anything you like. Only works and characters approved by their original creators can be used. The Help page also explains that the service has permission to use the original works it features through formal agreements with their creators. This is the foundation that lets you enjoy freely imagining “what if.”\n\nThe service first offered two works and four characters in Japan. “Taking part in a story” here means moving the story forward through conversation or making a story as a fan. The fun of reading a work is joined by the fun of thinking up what happens next.\n\nUntil now, “If it were me, I’d do it this way” was something you could only say to yourself. With byUs, those words become a way into making a story. What will you say to a character you love? What will happen next in the story? So, where will your “next part” begin?\n\n## In one line\nLINE Manga has launched byUs, an AI service that lets readers chat with approved characters and create stories based on their works. It gives readers a way to imagine what happens next and make fan stories they can keep private or share.\n\n\n【匿名の選定結果】\n\nS1:\n  1. blurted that out\n  2. take a step from A\n  3. thinking up something\n  4. before you know it\n  5. bring in something\n\nS2:\n  1. blurted ~ out\n\nS3:\n  1. think up\n  2. blurt\n  3. bring in\n  4. story-maker\n  5. can't wait\n\nS4:\n  1. blurted that out\n  2. find yourself thinking\n  3. formal agreements with their creators\n  4. moving the story forward\n  5. thinking up what happens next\n\nS5:\n  1. blurted something out\n  2. before you know it\n  3. approved by their original creators\n  4. make a story public\n  5. thinking up what happens next\n\nS6:\n  1. blurted that out\n  2. thinking up what happens next\n  3. before you know it\n  4. find yourself thinking\n  5. bring in just anything\n\nS7:\n  1. blurted that out\n  2. before you know it\n  3. bring in just anything\n  4. thinking up what happens next\n  5. a way into making a story\n"
